{
  "$schema": "gate-4f heading localization config",
  "$doc": [
    "Gate 4f — untranslated heading detection. Data only; the gate contains no string tests.",
    "",
    "markers[locale]: English heading tokens that appear in the EN rendered headings at",
    "  least 3x AND appear in ZERO rendered headings of that locale. Derived from the",
    "2,055-heading-per-locale rendered corpus at P35 and then FROZEN. Freezing is",
    "  load-bearing: if the list were re-derived at run time, introducing an English",
    "  heading would add its own tokens to the locale vocabulary and delete the very",
    "  markers that should have caught it. Regenerate only deliberately, never in CI.",
    "  Tokens legitimately shared with the target language self-exclude, which is why",
    "  `camping`/`guide` are absent for de/fr and `vernal`/`utah`/`gorge` for all.",
    "",
    "licensed: proper nouns that may appear in English in any locale. Seeded from the",
    "  headings that survived localization into ja/zh unchanged — the corpus itself",
    "  attesting they are not translatable — plus the A5/A6/C4 glossary locks. Matched",
    "  as whole phrases and stripped before tokenizing, so a compound heading such as",
    "  \"Red Cloud Loop vs Sheep Creek Geological Loop\" reduces to nothing and passes.",
    "",
    "state: `complete` makes findings blocking for that locale; `in-progress` demotes",
    "  them to warnings. A locale registered in i18n.ts with no entry here is a hard",
    "  exit 2 — never a silent pass (the ja UI-chrome fail-open lesson, handoff §7 4a)."
  ],
